# LiveFlows environment variables
#
# Copy to .env.local and fill in. .env.local is gitignored; this file is not.
# Never put real values in this file.
#
# Reference: docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-08-liveflows-design.md section 2

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Clerk — identity and organizations
# Dashboard → API keys.  https://dashboard.clerk.com
#
# Enable Organizations before running the app, or orgId is always undefined:
#   Dashboard → Organizations settings, or `clerk enable orgs`
# Choose "Membership required" so users route through the choose-organization
# session task. The app has no hand-built workspace picker.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
CLERK_SECRET_KEY=

# Generated when you create the webhook endpoint, so this stays empty until
# Wave 2. Locally, get a relay URL with:
#   clerk webhooks listen --token "$(clerk webhooks token)" \
#     --forward-to http://localhost:3000/api/webhooks/clerk
# Register that URL in the Dashboard, then copy its signing secret here.
# Read automatically by verifyWebhook() — do not pass it manually.
CLERK_WEBHOOK_SIGNING_SECRET=


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Postgres — Supabase is ONLY the database host
# Supabase → Connect
#
# No anon key, no service-role key, no Supabase JS client, no Supabase Auth,
# no RLS. Prisma owns data access; authorization lives in src/server/dal.
#
# Both values must be direct postgresql:// strings. Prisma 7 driver adapters
# reject prisma:// and prisma+postgres:// URLs — if you see either, you copied
# the Accelerate URL rather than the Postgres one.
#
# These two are NOT interchangeable:
#   DATABASE_URL  pooler host, port 6543, transaction mode — used at runtime
#   DIRECT_URL    pooler host, port 5432, session mode     — used by migrations
# prisma migrate fails against 6543 because migrations need session mode.
#
# On current Supabase both URLs share the same *.pooler.supabase.com host and
# differ only by port. Do not go looking for a separate db.*.supabase.co host —
# that is the older direct-connection format.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
DATABASE_URL=
DIRECT_URL=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 21st.dev — AI component library & CLI authentication
# https://21st.dev/mcp
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
API_KEY_21ST=


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Hocuspocus collaboration server (replaces Liveblocks realtime)
# See docs/specs/0007-realtime-migration.md
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_COLLAB_URL  Browser-facing WebSocket URL (wss://...).
#                         The reverse proxy routes /collab to the collab service.
# COLLAB_INTERNAL_URL     App → collab server URL over the internal Docker network.
#                         Used by MCP draw_elements to write Yjs documents.
# COLLAB_PORT             Internal listen port for the collab server. Default: 1234.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
NEXT_PUBLIC_COLLAB_URL=
COLLAB_INTERNAL_URL=ws://collab:1234
COLLAB_PORT=1234
